<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>UV-Safe</title>
    <link rel = "stylesheet" href ="/styles/main.css">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>

    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<!--"DM Serif Display", serif;-->
<!--"Plus Jakarta Sans", sans-serif;-->
<!--"Inter", sans-serif;-->

<body>
    <header>

        <div class="header-content">

            <a href="/" class="logo">UV☀️Safe</a>
            <nav class="about">
                <a href="/about">About</a>
            </nav>
        </div>     
    </header>

    <main class="about-section">

        <div class="about-card">

            <h1>About UV☀️Safe</h1>

            <p>
                UV-Safe is a simple website that helps you understand the
                ultraviolet (UV) level in a location and if you
                should consider using sunscreen.
            </p>

            <p>
                Enter a location and UV-Safe checks the available UV
                information for that area. It shows the current UV index,
                today's peak UV level, and the expected peak time.
            </p>

            <p>
                The goal is to make UV information easy to understand,
                so you can make informed decisions when spending
                time outdoors.
            </p>

            <div class="about-note">
                <strong>Stay informed. Stay protected. ☀️</strong>
            </div>

        </div>

    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
        <p>
            UV☀️Safe
        </p>

        <p>
            © <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> JanetOkedoyin
        </p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>